      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Considering how it seems like doing this doesn't disconnect the client anymore, all that forcing us to use TeleportTo does now is make us encounter weird bugs with single frame hitching when looking down to about 30 degrees and up to about 330.\n\nSo considering how basic of a function it is and that you can do a flawed version of it already, I don't see why it shouldn't exist.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-11-11T13:29:58.537Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Using SetVelocity, we can move the local player around, although a MovePosition() function is missing. But we can't rotate the player. Abusing TeleportTo for that disconnects the client for 'unusual behaviour'. \nA MoveRotation() function is needed. \nFurthermore, there should be a function that applies an offset velocity/rotation so that the player movement input is not overridden by the world rotation/position movement. This would allow concepts like walking around on moving objects, escalators, walkable vehicles etc.",
